codex
Baseline is green (webapp: vitest 45/45 passed, `vite build` succeeded; desktop: `node --check` passed on main.js/preload.js/release.js) and all frontend↔backend contracts I checked (meetings session/events/messages/advance, control run_now/save_settings, knowledge_drafts, mailbox, dashboard) match. However, the slice contains two P2 functional defects in default flows — the meetings page never exits the finished live-room view in rounds mode, and the free-meeting live room silently misses messages written during an SSE disconnect gap — plus several P3 dead-code/UX issues, so the patch should not be considered fully correct until those are addressed.

Full review comments:

- [P2] Refetch full message history after SSE reconnect in useMeetingStream — E:\code\novel-editorial\webapp\src\lib\use-meeting-stream.js:80-81
  The hook's own doc comment promises "重连后依赖消息表为真相（SSE 只做增量）", but `es.onerror` (webapp/src/lib/use-meeting-stream.js:80-81) only sets an error string: there is no `onopen` handler and no re-call of `getMeetingMessages(sessionId)` when EventSource reconnects. Any `message` events published while the connection is down (e.g. the desktop main.js auto-restart of the API after a crash) are written to `meeting_messages` but never pulled into the live view, so they stay missing until a full page reload; the "实时连接中断" badge also persists after a successful reconnect.

- [P2] Clear finished session so meetings page returns to start form — E:\code\novel-editorial\webapp\src\pages\MeetingsPage.jsx:99-100
  In rounds mode (the default), after the user clicks 结束会议 (`advance(true)`) or the backend finishes/fails the session, the poll at webapp/src/pages/MeetingsPage.jsx:99-100 detects `finished`/`failed` and calls `clearInterval(timer); refresh()` but never `setSession(null)`. The page stays stuck on the finished live-room view (badge 已完成, input row and 结束会议 button still rendered), and the 发起会议 form only returns after navigating away and back or reloading — `advance` on a finished session then fails with "当前状态不是等待输入". Free mode is unaffected because `FreeLive` calls `onEnded`.

- [P2] Commit version bump in desktop release script before tagging — E:\code\novel-editorial\desktop\release.js:132-133
  desktop/release.js:70-76 writes the bumped version into `desktop/package.json` via `writePackageVersion`, but the script never runs `git add`/`git commit` before `git tag v${version}` + `git push origin v${version}` (lines 132-133). The pushed tag therefore points to a tree whose package.json still has the old version, while the built installer embeds the new one. On a fresh clone at that tag the next `node release.js` bumps from the stale version and is rejected by the stale-version guard ("refusing to release stale version"), so the release pipeline breaks until the bump is manually committed.

- [P3] Remove dead closeToTray IPC channel in desktop preload — E:\code\novel-editorial\desktop\preload.js:11-11
  desktop/preload.js:11 exposes `closeToTray: () => ipcRenderer.send("app:close-to-tray")`, but `rg` shows no `ipcMain.on("app:close-to-tray", ...)` anywhere in desktop/main.js and no renderer code calls it — the channel is dead. The exposed API misleads future callers into thinking close-to-tray is handled (the actual hide-to-tray path is the `win:close` handler), so either register the listener or drop the binding.

- [P3] Load knowledge for initially selected novel in WorksPage — E:\code\novel-editorial\webapp\src\pages\WorksPage.jsx:35-44
  webapp/src/pages/WorksPage.jsx:35-44 calls `loadKnowledge` only inside `pick()`, while `selected` defaults to `novels[0]` without any effect. For the first (or URL-default) novel, the 知识库 tab renders `<LoadingState rows={3}/>` forever (`knowledge === null`, line 191) until the user manually clicks another project — the knowledge for the visible novel is never fetched.

- [P3] Wire or remove no-op 新建项目 button in WorksPage — E:\code\novel-editorial\webapp\src\pages\WorksPage.jsx:52-52
  webapp/src/pages/WorksPage.jsx:52 renders `<Button size="sm">新建项目</Button>` with no `onClick` handler — clicking it does nothing. The surrounding page has no project-creation flow, so this is a dead control that either needs an implementation or should be removed to avoid a fake action.

- [P3] Remove unused API wrappers and store fields (dead code) — E:\code\novel-editorial\webapp\src\api.js:121-129
  A large part of the API surface is never consumed: `subscribeEvents`, `exportNovels`, `getAiTaste`, `getEndingStatus`, `confirmNextBook`, `bindBook`, `createBookOnFanqie`, `deleteBookOnFanqie`, `getCharacterEvolution`, `getAgentStates`, `updateDiary`, `updateAgentState`, `getActivity`, `getAgentActions`, `updateAgentAction`, `createAgentAction`, `claimAction`, `getMemories`, `readKnowledge`, `saveKnowledge`, `distillLessons`, `actOnDraft` in webapp/src/api.js (e.g. lines 56-62, 87, 101-102, 121-129, 141-172) plus `liveSnapshot`/`setLiveSnapshot` in webapp/src/stores.js:7,14 — `rg` confirms each appears only at its definition. They duplicate backend endpoints the UI no longer uses, so keep the maintenance surface honest by deleting them (or restoring the pages that need them).

- [P3] Set created_at for SSE live messages in meeting stream — E:\code\novel-editorial\webapp\src\lib\use-meeting-stream.js:57-57
  Messages appended from SSE events are built with `created_at: ""` (webapp/src/lib/use-meeting-stream.js:57), so every live message in the free-meeting room renders an empty timestamp in FreeLive until a full reload populates the row from the DB. The event payload has no timestamp to copy, so either include one server-side or show the local receive time.
